.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt RAND_SET_DRBG_TYPE 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm RAND_set_DRBG_type ,
.Nm RAND_set_seed_source_type
.Nd specify the global random number generator types
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/rand.h
.Ft int
.Fo RAND_set_DRBG_type
.Fa "OSSL_LIB_CTX *ctx"
.Fa "const char *drbg"
.Fa "const char *propq"
.Fa "const char *cipher"
.Fa "const char *digest"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo RAND_set_seed_source_type
.Fa "OSSL_LIB_CTX *ctx"
.Fa "const char *seed"
.Fa "const char *propq"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn RAND_set_DRBG_type
specifies the random bit generator that will be used within the library
context
.Fa ctx .
A generator of name
.Fa drbg
with properties
.Fa propq
will be fetched.
It will be instantiated with either
.Fa cipher
or
.Fa digest
as its underlying cryptographic algorithm.
This specifies the type that will be used for the primary, public and
private random instances.
.Pp
.Fn RAND_set_seed_source_type
specifies the seed source that will be used within the library context
.Fa ctx .
The seed source of name
.Fa seed
with properties
.Fa propq
will be fetched and used to seed the primary random bit generator.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
These function return 1 on success and 0 on failure.
.Sh NOTES
These functions must be called before the random bit generators are
first created in the library context.
They will return an error if the call is made too late.
.Pp
The default DRBG is "CTR-DRBG" using the "AES-256-CTR" cipher.
.Pp
The default seed source can be configured when OpenSSL is compiled by
setting
.Sy -DOPENSSL_DEFAULT_SEED_SRC=SEED-SRC .
If not set then "SEED-SRC" is used.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal
 unsigned char bytes[100];
 RAND_set_seed_source_type(NULL, "JITTER", NULL);
 RAND_bytes(bytes, 100);
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr EVP_RAND 3 ,
.Xr RAND_get0_primary 3
.Sh HISTORY
These functions were added in OpenSSL 3.0.
